# This kernel had no console at all: llvm-nm on the 27 build defines only
# _k60_serial_clock next to the 16 build's _k60_usblog_console_up and
# _pong_ramoops_console_*. Without a mirror nothing the kernel says is
# readable, so every 0-byte flight was uninformative by construction. The
# 16-series guard asked for -DPONG, which this build never defines. The first
# cut here guarded with XNU_PONG_RAMOOPS_CONSOLE and passed -D through the env
# prefix of the kernel step; the define never reached the compiler (P-301:
# serial_console.o.json carried zero occurrences while startup.o.json carried
# the builder's own EXTRA_MAKE_ARGS define), so the kernel shipped with no
# console a third time. The hooks are now compiled unconditionally and guard
# themselves at run time on pong_ramoops_base. Base 0xa7000000 and the 2 MiB
# window are the device live FDT ramoops node (reg 0x400000, pmsg-size 0x200000).
